# REBASH Academy Hands-on Lab System

## Canonical lab mandate (mandatory)

Follow `.cursor/prompts/tutorials/create_lab.md` and `.cursor/rules/00-foundation/09-content-quality-standard.mdc`.

Labs must be real-world, topic-specific, and **copy-paste executable** end-to-end.

Required core: Objective · Prerequisites · Lab environment · Real-world scenario · Step-by-step tasks (Expected output each) · Validation · Common errors · Challenge (working artefact) · Learning outcomes · Cleanup.

**Ban:** note-taking / runbook.md challenges; generic host-baseline templates reused across unrelated topics; placeholder `# TODO` commands.

Prefer Codex until the user changes agents.

## Purpose

This rule defines how hands-on labs should be generated.

Labs transform theoretical knowledge into practical engineering skills.

Every lab should simulate real-world engineering work.

Learners should leave every lab with practical confidence.

